<title>GERMANY: Dell sees strong Q3 growth after &quot;astronomical&quot; Q2.</title>
<headline>Dell sees strong Q3 growth after &quot;astronomical&quot; Q2.</headline>
<byline>John Gilardi</byline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dell Computer Corp, the U.S. computer maker, believes its third quarter is &quot;looking strong&quot; and still expects robust worldwide personal computer industry sales, a top company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seeing closer to 20 percent worldwide. In the U.S., of course, it is more heavily saturated, so 13 percent overall market growth is probably not out of line,&quot; Eric Harslem, senior vice president of the product group at Dell, said in an interview with Reuters.</p>
</text>
